-- title:
--   Admissibility of the cyclic space of a spherical Whittaker function
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field whose ring of integers is an integral $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$-algebra and with $[K:\mathbb Q]=3$, and let $\mu\colon(\mathbb A_K)^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$ be a group homomorphism with $\|\mu(x)\|=1$ for all $x$. Fix a nonzero prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ and a function $W$ on $\mathrm{LocalGL3}\,v=\mathrm{GL}_3$ of the completion of $\mathbb Q$ at $v$, and assume `IsInducedSphericalAt` holds for $W$ with coefficient function `inducedCoeff K μ` (the value $\mu$ of a uniformizer idele at an unramified prime of $\mathcal O_K$, and $0$ at the ramified ones) and with the subgroup `localMaximalCompact3` of matrices all of whose entries, and all of whose inverse's entries, have valuation $\le 1$: that is, $W$ is invariant under right translation by that subgroup, is a Hecke coset eigenfunction for $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_v,1,1)$ with eigenvalue $\mathrm{cNormQ}(v)\cdot\mathrm{inducedE1}$ and for $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_v,\varpi_v,1)$ with eigenvalue $\mathrm{cNormQ}(v)\cdot\mathrm{inducedE2}$, where $\mathrm{cNormQ}(v)$ is the absolute norm of $v$, and satisfies $W(\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_v,\varpi_v,\varpi_v)g)=\mathrm{inducedE3}\cdot W(g)$. Assume further that $\psi_v$ is an additive character of the completion with $W(u(x,y,z)g)=\psi_v(x+y)W(g)$ for all $x,y,z$ and all $g$, where $u(x,y,z)$ is the upper triangular unipotent matrix with entries $x,y,z$, that `addCharLevel` $\psi_v=0$, and that $\psi_v\neq 1$. Then for every subgroup $U_v$ of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ that is open as a set there is a finite set $B$ of complex-valued functions on $\mathrm{GL}_3$ such that every $F$ in `gl3CyclicSubspace W`, the $\mathbb C$-span of the right translates of $W$, satisfying $F(gk)=F(g)$ for all $k\in U_v$ and all $g$, lies in the $\mathbb C$-span of $B$.
--
--   This is the admissibility statement for the representation generated by the spherical $\psi_v$-Whittaker function attached at $v$ to the cubic induction of $\mu$: each space of $U_v$-fixed vectors in the cyclic space of $W$ is finite-dimensional, being controlled by a finite family of functions. It is obtained by identifying the cyclic space inside a principal series of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over the completion of $\mathbb Q$ at $v$, and it feeds the local analysis of zeta integrals and the Rankin–Selberg estimates used later in the Langlands–Tunnell argument.
